{"id": "EUVD-2026-108925", "enisaUuid": "1d6a56d0-35d9-3e3e-b9e1-a319265277cd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nriscv: ptrace: Zero-initialize regset buffers before copyin\n\nuser_regset_copyin() only copies `count` bytes, so a PTRACE_SETREGSET\nrequest with a short iov_len leaves the rest of the stack buffer\nuninitialized. In riscv_vr_set() that garbage is validated and copied\ninto the target's vstate, and in riscv_cfi_set() it can be stored as\nthe target's shadow stack pointer. Zero both buffers, as the get path\nalready does.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:19:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:19:10", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/89fc70d73f4ac8781f9e15edd1dbc6b6088453b3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/59052a88ba5fe4a7bb34b3a0a42aa5d453d3bb97"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98951"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d9eb9bf-fd4c-3c10-8b83-dd3b78570d7d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9300f00439743c4a34d735e1a27118eb68a1504e <89fc70d73f4ac8781f9e15edd1dbc6b6088453b3"}, {"id": "3cb7a3ca-2230-3e40-b820-6fe604bf5416", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "751aee69-70b5-3b06-b911-6073dc383ad0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f2a9cd050901c4734bc175294c3bd6a40a1a9e99"}, {"id": "77df7fbd-a7a9-3d6a-b9e1-c641fb638051", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "90e8a497-0cce-318f-b558-ac924c906559", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9300f00439743c4a34d735e1a27118eb68a1504e <59052a88ba5fe4a7bb34b3a0a42aa5d453d3bb97"}, {"id": "b7c76dff-ed47-3e4c-b04d-7d3b07a2290d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "bfde10dc-3a02-3599-a1ac-b8b6e8dc260d", "prod